{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-11-03_d897437dex991.htm, sha256 89b3df041613aefbecf493b2b14914fc4d1669e54bc23a21320e80ab35db30d8.\nEX-99.1 2 d897437dex991.htm EX-99.1\nExhibit 99.1\nCVR Energy Reports Third Quarter 2026 Results\n\u2022\nSeparately announced today a definitive agreement to acquire Marathon Petroleum Corporation\u2019s St. Paul Park and Mandan refineries and related marketing business\n\u2022\nThird quarter 2026 net income attributable to CVR Energy stockholders of $570 million; Adjusted EBITDA of $582 million\n\u2022\n$253 million liability removed from balance sheet due to the EPA\u2019s August 2026 decision granting a full waiver for Wynnewood Refining Company, LLC (\u201cWRC\u201d) for the 2025 compliance period\n\u2022\nDeclared cash dividend of 10 cents for the third quarter 2026\n\u2022\nCVR Partners, LP (\u201cCVR Partners\u201d) announced a third quarter 2026 cash distribution of $1.79 per common unit\nSUGAR LAND, Texas (November 3, 2026) \u2013 CVR Energy, Inc. (\u201cCVR Energy\u201d or the \u201cCompany\u201d) (NYSE: CVI) today announced its third quarter 2026 results including a net income attributable to CVR Energy stockholders of $570 million, or $5.67 per diluted share, and an adjusted earnings per diluted share of $4.00, compared to net income attributable to CVR Energy stockholders of $374 million, or $3.72 per diluted share, and an adjusted earnings per diluted share of 40 cents for the third quarter of 2025. Net income for the third quarter of 2026 was $563 million compared to net income of $401 million for the third quarter of 2025. Adjusted EBITDA for the third quarter of 2026 was $582 million compared to $180 million for the third quarter of 2025.\n\u201cWe are incredibly excited about our announcements this morning of a definitive agreement to acquire two high quality refineries from Marathon Petroleum, along with the associated marketing and logistics assets,\u201d said Dane Neumann, CVR Energy\u2019s President and Chief Executive Officer. \u201cWe also announced the best quarterly results in the Company\u2019s history on both a consolidated basis and in the Petroleum segment, driven by strong operations across our system and record crack spreads. We are also pleased to announce a quarterly dividend of 10 cents per share. Looking ahead, we remain optimistic about the near-term outlook while we seek to close on our transformative transaction with Marathon Petroleum by the end of the year.\u201d\n\u201cCVR Partners\u2019 results for the third quarter were impacted by the planned turnaround at its East Dubuque facility, which was completed in mid-October as scheduled,\u201d Neumann continued. \u201cDespite the downtime associated with the turnaround, CVR Partners had another quarter of solid results and declared a cash distribution of $1.79 per common unit for the third quarter.\u201d\nSegment Highlights\nBelow are financial and operational highlights of each of the Company\u2019s reportable segments:\nThree Months Ended\nSeptember 30, Nine Months Ended\nSeptember 30,\n2026 2025 2026 2025\nPetroleum Segment\nPetroleum net income (in millions)\n$ 746 $ 520 $ 565 $ 223\n"}
